{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Or in robbery, or having oppressed his fellow.</b> There is a distinction between גזל (robbery) and עושק (oppression), and this is what is written (Leviticus 19:13) ״לא תעשק את רעך ולא תגזול״ — each one specified in its own separate prohibition, for they are two things: גזל is where he admits that the seized property is in his hand but he does not wish to return it to him; עשק is where he denies it and says, 'I have already returned it to you,' or 'I have already paid you your wages.' And this is what is said in Bava Metzi'a (111a): What is גזל and what is עשק? 'I have it in my possession and I do not give it to you' — this is גזל; 'I have already given it to you' — this is עשק."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:05.613366617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}